insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('19bea673-c1df-5e3a-b681-673831efe452', 'wg12-informative-writing-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-informative-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Goalball: A Sport Played by Sound$q$, $q$(1) Goalball is a team sport designed for athletes with visual impairments, and it is played almost entirely by sound. (2) Two teams of three players face each other on a court about the size of a volleyball court, with a goal stretching across the full width of each end line. (3) Players take turns rolling a heavy rubber ball toward the opposing goal, while defenders dive sideways to block it with their bodies.

(4) The ball is the key to the game. (5) It contains small bells that jingle as it rolls, allowing defenders to track its path without seeing it. (6) To keep the competition fair, every player wears blackout eyeshades, so athletes with some vision gain no advantage over those with none. (7) Tactile lines, strips of tape laid over string, mark the court so players can feel their positions with their hands and feet.

(8) Because the players depend on hearing, spectators must stay silent while the ball is in play. (9) Fans may cheer only after a goal is scored or the referee stops play. (10) This rule surprises many first-time visitors, who are used to loud crowds at other sporting events.

(11) The sport has grown steadily. (12) At the 2024 Northgate Regional Championships, thirty-two teams competed, compared with nine teams at the first event in 2010. (13) My cousin went to a game once and said it was really quiet. (14) Coach Imani Lindqvist reported that the youth program at Lindqvist's club had doubled in size in five years.$q$, 'draft')
