   $q$In sentence 4, the writer compares the cable to a garden hose mainly to:$q$, $q$[{"text":"explain how the repeaters amplify light pulses","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"suggest that the cable carries water as well as data","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"help readers picture the cable's size by using a familiar object","is_correct":true},{"text":"show that the cable is easily damaged by gardeners","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$help readers picture the cable's size by using a familiar object$q$, $q$The comparison gives readers a concrete sense of how thin the cable is, which supports "surprisingly slender." Reading it as a claim that the cable carries water takes the comparison literally.$q$, 'draft', 'cee10173-2559-5bbe-bef4-df294d6d2c8c')
