   $q$A reviewer says the report makes varnish removal sound simpler than it is. Which addition best shows the complexity of the topic while keeping an objective tone?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Conservators sometimes leave a thin layer of old varnish in place, since removing every trace can endanger delicate paint layers beneath it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Some people think that old paintings should simply be left alone forever.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-opinion"},{"text":"Cotton swabs are sold in large packages at most stores.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Cleaning a painting is basically the hardest job anyone could ever have.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-overstatement"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Conservators sometimes leave a thin layer of old varnish in place, since removing every trace can endanger delicate paint layers beneath it.$q$, $q$The correct sentence adds a specific, objective limitation that shows conservators must balance competing risks. The "hardest job" sentence claims the work is difficult but is exaggerated and informal and gives no information.$q$, 'draft', 'c50f4846-0f1f-5c8d-8ec2-48ea194da042')
