   $q$Which revision of sentence 12 best shows the shift in time and setting at the start of the final paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"For instance, it was the championship meet, and our team was ready to run.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"example-not-time"},{"text":"Two weeks later, under the stadium lights at the championship meet, I took my place on the curve.","is_correct":true},{"text":"In contrast, it was the championship meet, and many teams had come to compete.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contrast-not-time"},{"text":"It was the championship meet, which is the most important meet of the whole season.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"explains-not-transitions"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Two weeks later, under the stadium lights at the championship meet, I took my place on the curve.$q$, $q$"Two weeks later" marks time and "under the stadium lights" places the reader in the new setting. "In contrast" signals an opposing idea rather than a move forward in time.$q$, 'draft', 'aa203434-f8ac-5def-8443-f0a04b3b03ff')
