   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence 13 as a conclusion that reflects on the experience?$q$, $q$[{"text":"There were three hundred and twelve graduates in the class that year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-detail"},{"text":"The ceremony ended at noon, and everyone went outside to take photographs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"flat-ending-no-reflection"},{"text":"Somewhere, a grandparent had read every name correctly, and that was worth the late night.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Captioning software has improved a great deal over the past several years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-fact-ending"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Somewhere, a grandparent had read every name correctly, and that was worth the late night.$q$, $q$The correct choice reflects on who benefited and ties the work in sentence 8 to the purpose in sentence 1. Photographs outside add an event but no reflection.$q$, 'draft', '8f0f64dc-fe36-5d75-abac-cdcc4eb28841')
