-- Passage wg12-narrative-writing-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('b6d6c2f9-3e24-5625-927f-10feea480caf', 'wg12-narrative-writing-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-narrative-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Line Set Twelve$q$, $q$(1) During the spring musical, I worked on the fly crew, the team that raises and lowers scenery from the pipes above the stage. (2) Each piece of scenery hangs on a line set, a system of ropes and counterweights that lets one person move a heavy backdrop smoothly. (3) My line set, number twelve, held a painted city skyline that had to drop in during the final song of the first act.

(4) On opening night, the stage manager, Ms. Abiodun, called the cue over my headset. (5) I pulled the rope. (6) Nothing moved. (7) The lock that holds the rope in place was still half closed, and the rope was jammed against it. (8) The cast was already singing the last chorus. (9) Our school has performed a spring musical every year for decades.

(10) I flipped the lock fully open, braced my feet, and pulled again. (11) The skyline dropped so fast that I had to grip the rope with both hands to slow it. (12) It stopped two feet above the stage floor, exactly on its mark, just as the final note ended.

(13) At intermission, Ms. Abiodun found me in the wings. (14) I was sure she was going to tell me I had nearly ruined the act. (15) Instead, she said, "Everyone misses a lock once. Most people freeze when it happens." (16) After that night, I checked every lock twice before every cue.$q$, 'draft')
