   $q$Which change would most weaken the logical sequence of events?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Combining sentences 10 and 11 into a single sentence joined by a comma and \"and.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"style-not-sequence"},{"text":"Moving sentence 8 to after sentence 12, so the realization comes after the new method.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Changing \"Last fall\" in sentence 1 to \"In September\" to name the month.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"detail-not-sequence"},{"text":"Moving sentence 3 into the second paragraph, right before sentence 4.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"minor-move-not-logic"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Moving sentence 8 to after sentence 12, so the realization comes after the new method.$q$, $q$Sentence 8 is the realization that causes the narrator to throw out the lesson in sentence 9, so placing it after the new method breaks cause and effect. Combining sentences 10 and 11 changes style but not the order of events.$q$, 'draft', '8284e33b-58a0-5813-9a59-c685ea9b21d6')
