   $q$The writer wants to add a concluding sentence after sentence 11. Which choice best concludes the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Public transportation has existed in some form in cities around the world for well over a century.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-broad"},{"text":"By gathering evidence and proposing a change that cost nothing, the council showed that students can improve a service the whole town depends on.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The adult riders who worked late shifts said the later buses made their evenings much less stressful.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Next year, the council hopes to survey students about the lunch menu and the length of passing periods between classes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By gathering evidence and proposing a change that cost nothing, the council showed that students can improve a service the whole town depends on.$q$, $q$The correct sentence sums up the council's survey, its cost-free proposal, and the town-wide benefit, so it closes the whole passage. The sentence about adult riders only extends one detail from sentence 11 and does not reflect the council's role.$q$, 'draft', 'e683a37d-9d9f-5316-b63f-451ab50b0507')
