   $q$A paragraph argues that runners should add swimming to their training. It explains that swimming builds endurance, strengthens muscles that running neglects, and reduces the pounding on knees and ankles. Which sentence best concludes the paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A few laps each week can make a runner stronger and more durable without adding strain to the joints.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Knees and ankles absorb several times a runner's body weight with every stride on pavement.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Running on soft trails is another way to protect the joints during long workouts.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"Some swimmers prefer the backstroke because it allows them to breathe more easily.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A few laps each week can make a runner stronger and more durable without adding strain to the joints.$q$, $q$The correct sentence pulls together endurance, strength, and joint protection, the three reasons the paragraph gives, and restates the argument. The sentence about knees and ankles supports only one reason, so it reads as a detail rather than a conclusion.$q$, 'draft', null)
