   $q$A traffic counter recorded about 1,200 cyclists on the new bike lanes each weekday. A report draft says: "Lots of people seem to sort of use the new bike lanes." Which revision is the most precise?$q$, $q$[{"text":"About 12,000 cyclists use the new bike lanes each weekday, according to a traffic counter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"changes-meaning"},{"text":"About 1,200 cyclists use the new bike lanes each weekday, according to a traffic counter.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Many people appear to use the new bike lanes fairly often.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-wording"},{"text":"A whole bunch of cyclists ride the new bike lanes every weekday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$About 1,200 cyclists use the new bike lanes each weekday, according to a traffic counter.$q$, $q$The correct revision replaces the vague "lots of people seem to sort of" with the exact figure and its source. The 12,000 choice is just as specific, but it misstates the number.$q$, 'draft', null)
