   $q$Read the sentence: "At 6 a.m. in the morning, the students launched a weather balloon that was filled with helium gas, and it rose up to an altitude of 30 kilometers in height." Which revision is the most concise while keeping every fact?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The students launched a helium-filled weather balloon that rose to 30 kilometers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drops-detail"},{"text":"At 6 a.m., the students initiated the release of a balloon containing helium, which ascended to 30 kilometers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"inflated-diction"},{"text":"At 6 a.m. in the morning, the students launched a helium balloon that rose up to 30 kilometers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"redundancy-remains"},{"text":"At 6 a.m., the students launched a helium-filled weather balloon that rose to 30 kilometers.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$At 6 a.m., the students launched a helium-filled weather balloon that rose to 30 kilometers.$q$, $q$The correct revision cuts "in the morning," "gas," "up," and "in height," all of which repeat ideas already stated, and keeps the time, the helium, and the altitude. The choice that begins "The students launched" is shorter still, but it drops the launch time.$q$, 'draft', null)
