   $q$Read the sentence: "The wind turbines on the ridge generate power for nearly two thousand homes ___ are quiet enough that hikers barely notice them." Which choice correctly completes the sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"homes, they","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"},{"text":"homes. They","is_correct":true},{"text":"homes and, they","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misplaced-comma-with-conjunction"},{"text":"homes they","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fused-sentence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$homes. They$q$, $q$A period separates the two independent clauses into two complete sentences. Using only a comma between them creates a comma splice, and using nothing creates a fused sentence.$q$, 'draft', null)
