   $q$Read the sentence: "The choir rehearsed the new piece for weeks, nevertheless, the harmonies in the final measure remained shaky." Which revision fixes the error?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The choir rehearsed the new piece for weeks nevertheless, the harmonies in the final measure remained shaky.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fused-sentence"},{"text":"The choir rehearsed the new piece for weeks, nevertheless the harmonies in the final measure remained shaky.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"conjunctive-adverb-with-comma-only"},{"text":"The choir rehearsed the new piece for weeks; nevertheless, the harmonies in the final measure remained shaky.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The choir rehearsed the new piece for weeks, nevertheless; the harmonies in the final measure remained shaky.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misplaced-semicolon"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The choir rehearsed the new piece for weeks; nevertheless, the harmonies in the final measure remained shaky.$q$, $q$"Nevertheless" is a conjunctive adverb, not a conjunction, so the clauses need a semicolon before it and a comma after it. Removing the second comma does nothing to fix the comma splice.$q$, 'draft', null)
