   $q$Read the sentences: "The ceramics studio fires its kiln twice a month. Usually on weekends when electricity rates are lower." Which revision fixes the fragment?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The ceramics studio fires its kiln twice a month. Usually, on weekends when electricity rates are lower.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fragment-unfixed"},{"text":"The ceramics studio fires its kiln twice a month, it is usually on weekends when electricity rates are lower.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"},{"text":"The ceramics studio fires its kiln twice a month; usually on weekends when electricity rates are lower.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-before-phrase"},{"text":"The ceramics studio fires its kiln twice a month, usually on weekends when electricity rates are lower.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The ceramics studio fires its kiln twice a month, usually on weekends when electricity rates are lower.$q$, $q$"Usually on weekends when electricity rates are lower" is a phrase that adds detail, so a comma attaches it to the main clause. A semicolon must be followed by an independent clause, which this phrase is not.$q$, 'draft', null)
