   $q$Which choice contains no comma splice, fused sentence, or fragment?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Although the bridge was rated for heavy trucks, engineers closed it for inspection after the flood the river had scoured away soil around two of its piers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fused-sentence"},{"text":"Although the bridge was rated for heavy trucks; engineers closed it for inspection after the flood, because the river had scoured away soil around two of its piers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-after-dependent-clause"},{"text":"Although the bridge was rated for heavy trucks, engineers closed it for inspection after the flood; the river had scoured away soil around two of its piers.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Although the bridge was rated for heavy trucks, engineers closed it for inspection after the flood, the river had scoured away soil around two of its piers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-unfixed"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Although the bridge was rated for heavy trucks, engineers closed it for inspection after the flood; the river had scoured away soil around two of its piers.$q$, $q$The semicolon after "flood" correctly separates two independent clauses, and the opening dependent clause is attached with a comma. The choice with a comma after "flood" joins "engineers closed it" and "the river had scoured" with only a comma, a comma splice.$q$, 'draft', null)
